+    <!-- 9. FAQ -->
+    <section id="faq">
+      <h2>9&nbsp; FAQ &amp; Troubleshooting</h2>
+
+      <h3>The dashboard shows "No active project" after I create one</h3>
+      <p>
+        The project is stored in the Streamlit session state. If the page fully reloads
+        (e.g. after a code change while the dev server is running), session state is cleared.
+        Simply re-create the project in the sidebar — this is expected behaviour for the MVP's
+        in-memory persistence.
+      </p>
+
+      <h3>Clicking "Load Mock Dataset" does nothing</h3>
+      <p>
+        Ensure the file
+        <code>RegulatoryGuardAI_Test_Records/RegulatoryGuardAI_mock_preclinical_data.csv</code>
+        exists relative to the directory you launched Streamlit from. Always run
+        <code>streamlit run app.py</code> from the project root.
+      </p>
+
+      <h3><code>ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'streamlit'</code></h3>
+      <p>
+        Your virtual environment is not active, or you forgot to run
+        <code>pip install -r requirements.txt</code>.
+        Re-activate the environment (<code>source .venv/bin/activate</code>) and reinstall.
+      </p>
+
+      <h3>Rules uploaded but compliance check still uses old thresholds</h3>
+      <p>
+        After uploading new rules, click <strong>"▶ Run Compliance Check"</strong> again.
+        Uploading the file updates the rules in session state; the engine only uses them
+        on the next run.
+      </p>
+
+      <h3>Bob 2.0 returns an error or empty text</h3>
+      <ul>
+        <li>Verify the endpoint URL is correct and includes the full path (e.g. <code>/v1/text/generation</code>).</li>
+        <li>Confirm the API key is valid and has not expired.</li>
+        <li>Check that your network allows outbound HTTPS to the IBM Cloud endpoint.</li>
+        <li>If the issue persists, the placeholder narrative is used automatically — the app remains fully functional.</li>
+      </ul>
+
+      <h3>How do I add my own cohort-to-rule mappings?</h3>
+      <p>
+        Open <code>app.py</code> and find the <code>COHORT_RULE_MAP</code> dictionary near the top.
+        Add entries in the format <code>"Your_Cohort_Name": "Assay_Parameter_Name"</code>.
+        The assay parameter name must exactly match the <code>Assay_Parameter</code> column value
+        in your rules CSV.
+      </p>
+
+      <h3>I want to persist projects across sessions</h3>
+      <p>
+        The MVP uses Streamlit session state (in-memory). For persistence, export the results CSV
+        after each session. A database backend is out of scope for this hackathon release.
+      </p>
+
+      <h3>Port 8501 is already in use</h3>
+      <pre><code>streamlit run app.py --server.port 8080</code></pre>
+
+      <h3>Python version compatibility</h3>
